<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN>

<PLUGIN
  name="fanctrlplus2"
  author="ck9393 / andrebrait"
  version="1.9.0"
  launch="Settings/fanctrlplus2"
  pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/andrebrait/fanctrlplus/main/plugin/fanctrlplus2.plg"
  min="6.9.0"
  support="https://github.com/andrebrait/fanctrlplus/issues"
  project="https://github.com/andrebrait/fanctrlplus"
  readme="https://github.com/andrebrait/fanctrlplus#readme"
>

<ICON>
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/fanctrlplus2/images/fanctrlplus2.png
</ICON>

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[

### 1.9.0

## What's changed

- Discover PWM channels numbered 10 and above, exclude per-channel attributes such as `pwm10_enable`, and list channels in natural numeric order. Older driver layouts remain supported. (#10)
- Preserve fan labels and group assignments across hwmon renumbering and USB HID re-enumeration instead of leaving them attached to vanished sysfs paths. (#12)
- Record unique USB controller serial identities so assignments follow controllers across USB port, bus, and hub changes, even when an identical model occupies the old port. Controllers without a unique serial retain separate same-port bindings.
- Keep missing or ambiguous controller bindings for recovery without controlling another device, and prevent multiple configurations from driving the same PWM channel.
- Preserve unresolved bindings across configuration saves and renames. Clearing a label also removes its dormant identity entry so it cannot reappear when ambiguity is resolved.

## Upgrade compatibility

Back up `/boot/config/plugins/fanctrlplus2/` before upgrading, especially if you may need to downgrade later. No manual conversion is needed for controllers still identifiable at their saved location: their bindings are upgraded when the service starts.

Start the service on 1.9.0 **before moving a USB controller** so its serial can be recorded. If an older, unrecorded controller has already moved, reassign it once. Controllers without a unique serial must remain on the same USB port. Restart the service after a driver reload or USB port move; this release does not add hot-plug monitoring.

Older plugin versions do not understand the new serial-based label keys. Restore your pre-upgrade configuration backup if downgrading. Device identity identifies the controller's channel, not the physical fan plugged into it.

The export/import request in #11 remains separate and is not included in this release.

## Verification

All 25 test files pass. Isolated runtime smoke checks exercised actual label/configuration endpoints and service startup against synthetic sysfs, including port moves with replacements, ambiguous identities, recovery, saves, and label deletion. Physical hardware validation is still welcome.

Thanks to @mrjacobarussell for the multi-channel fix and detailed ARCTIC controller reports.

### 1.8.3

## What's changed

- Fix the plugin's description on the **Plugins** page. Unraid builds that column from the README packaged inside the plugin, and the release was packaging the project's README, so the description was the whole thing — badges, install instructions and licence notes in a table cell. It is now a description written for that column.

## Upgrade compatibility

Existing configurations continue to work and need no migration. Nothing about fan control changes; this affects only the text Unraid shows for the plugin itself.

### 1.8.2

## What's changed

- Fix the reorder arrows on the first and last fan configuration. The disabled one could point a different way from the working one beside it — a left arrow next to a down arrow — and a page showing a single configuration used left and right on a phone.

Which arrow a button shows is now a question about the layout alone, answered once for the whole page: along the row where configurations sit side by side, down the column where they do not. Whether the button works stays a question about where its configuration sits in the list. The two no longer influence each other.

## Upgrade compatibility

Existing configurations continue to work and need no migration. This changes only which arrow is drawn on the reorder buttons; reordering itself, and everything else, behaves as it did in 1.8.1.


For older releases, see https://github.com/andrebrait/fanctrlplus/releases
]]>
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
old_manifest="/boot/config/plugins/fanctrlplus.plg"
old_runtime="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/fanctrlplus"
old_config="/boot/config/plugins/fanctrlplus"
new_config="/boot/config/plugins/fanctrlplus2"
marker="$new_config/.migration-v1"

if [[ ! -e "$marker" ]]; then
  mkdir -p "$new_config"

  if [[ -d "$old_config" ]]; then
    for old_cfg in "$old_config"/fanctrlplus_*.cfg; do
      [[ -f "$old_cfg" ]] || continue
      old_name="${old_cfg##*/}"
      new_cfg="$new_config/fanctrlplus2_${old_name#fanctrlplus_}"
      [[ -e "$new_cfg" ]] || cp -p "$old_cfg" "$new_cfg"
    done

    if [[ -f "$old_config/order.cfg" && ! -e "$new_config/order.cfg" ]]; then
      sed 's/fanctrlplus_/fanctrlplus2_/g' "$old_config/order.cfg" > "$new_config/order.cfg.tmp" &&
        mv "$new_config/order.cfg.tmp" "$new_config/order.cfg"
    fi

    if [[ -f "$old_config/pwm_labels.cfg" && ! -e "$new_config/pwm_labels.cfg" ]]; then
      cp -p "$old_config/pwm_labels.cfg" "$new_config/pwm_labels.cfg"
    fi
  fi

  touch "$marker"
fi

if [[ -f "$old_manifest" || -d "$old_runtime" ]]; then
  echo ""
  echo "FanCtrl Plus configuration imported into FanCtrl Plus 2."
  echo "Uninstall upstream FanCtrl Plus, then install FanCtrl Plus 2 again."
  echo "Installation stopped to prevent both plugins controlling the same fans."
  echo ""
  exit 1
fi

exit 0
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/fanctrlplus2/fanctrlplus2-1.9.0-noarch-1.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new --reinstall">
<URL>https://github.com/andrebrait/fanctrlplus/releases/download/1.9.0/fanctrlplus2-1.9.0-noarch-1.txz</URL>
<SHA256>04092b991c8112f483552f6ca27dd40f8420b233c05e886cb791c7efcc2447cd</SHA256>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
for package in /boot/config/plugins/fanctrlplus2/fanctrlplus2-*.txz; do
  [[ "$package" == "/boot/config/plugins/fanctrlplus2/fanctrlplus2-1.9.0-noarch-1.txz" ]] || rm -f "$package"
done

src="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/fanctrlplus2/scripts/rc.fanctrlplus2"
dst="/etc/rc.d/rc.fanctrlplus2"
if [[ -f "$src" ]]; then
  ln -sf "$src" "$dst"
fi

mkdir -p /var/tmp/fanctrlplus2
rm -f /var/tmp/fanctrlplus2/*
pkill -f "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/fanctrlplus2/scripts/array_monitor.sh"

if [[ -x "$dst" ]]; then
  "$dst" restart
fi

script="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/fanctrlplus2/scripts/array_monitor.sh"
if [[ -x "$script" ]]; then
  nohup "$script" >/dev/null 2>&1 &
fi

echo ""
echo "------------------------------------------------"
echo " FanCtrl Plus 2 is installed."
echo " Version: 1.9.0"
echo "------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
exit 0
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/fanctrlplus2/scripts/rc.fanctrlplus2 stop 2>/dev/null
pkill -f "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/fanctrlplus2/scripts/array_monitor.sh"
removepkg fanctrlplus2 2>/dev/null || true

rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/fanctrlplus2
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/fanctrlplus2
rm -f /etc/rc.d/rc.fanctrlplus2

echo "============================================================"
echo "    FanCtrl Plus 2 has been removed."
echo "    Reboot to restore fan control to BIOS or other tools."
echo "============================================================"
exit 0
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
